  "notes": "Compton’s drum-first producer, working across Dr. Dre-orbit rap, pop and K-pop — the widest stylistic range in this section. The research is unambiguous that **the drums are the identity**: he came up playing drums in church, and the records are heavy, live-feel, gospel-derived kit programming — ghost 16ths and rimshots on the backbeat, busy kick patterns with two or three hits a bar. Harmony is minor with industrial colour: static beds, chromatic stabs, and the abrupt key and section changes carried over from his pop work. ⚠ `medium`: background, drum lineage and credits are documented; harmonic detail inferred `[LOW-CONF]`.",
